WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.060
If you are familiar with knitting slip
stitch patterns on the single bed,

2
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.660
multi-colored slip is
the next logical step.

3
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.980
While knitting in slip selected needles

4
00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:16.100
do not knit and the working yarn travels
under the needles creating floats

5
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:21.460
on the purl side of the knitting.
By changing colors every two rows,

6
00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:23.780
a design is created on the knit side

7
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.660
of the knitting, allowing
multiple colors across the row.

8
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:30.900
The slip stitches are carried across

9
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:36.860
the alternating colors,
creating interesting graphic elements.

10
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:41.580
The best way to understand multicolored
slip is to knit it in two contrasting

11
00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:45.620
colors and examine the stitches
that are slipping.

12
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:49.700
You don't need a color changer
to knit 2-color slip.

13
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:55.800
You could manually change the yarn every
two rows to get an idea of how this works.

